        "domain": 0.0,
        "chosen": true,
        "text": "Wrote the dissertation's AI-agent sections covering architecture, implementation and evaluation, including a documented hallucination-rate analysis and test-case outcomes."
      },
      {
        "id": "az10",
        "entry": "AstraZeneca",
        "score": 5.5,
        "keywords": 5.5,
        "domain": 0.0,
        "chosen": true,
        "text": "Needed an agent that researchers could trust on a cancer research platform, including when its tools fail: built a tool-calling agent (LangChain, Claude Haiku 4.5 on AWS Bedrock) for three use cases (gene alias resolution, prompt-engineered explanations of a fixed scoring pipeline, validated dataset descriptions), with deterministic Ensembl and HGNC calls, deterministic hallucination guards, and circuit breakers with a 19,213-gene parquet fallback for when the external APIs are unavailable."
      },
      {
        "id": "dc6",
        "entry": "180 Degrees Consulting Bristol",
        "score": 4.0,
        "keywords": 4.0,
        "domain": 0.0,
        "chosen": true,
        "text": "A product-startup client needed an agentic AI prototype turned into software their team could use: led the architecture for a five-person cross-functional team, designed hierarchical agent workflows (MCP, Exograph GraphQL, PostgreSQL for persistent storage and retrieval across agent sessions) and built the Python prototype (FastMCP, Ollama, GitHub Actions CI), then ran a live demo with client stakeholders (5-star rating from senior leadership) within the three-month engagement."
      },
      {
        "id": "az1",
        "entry": "AstraZeneca",
        "score": 3.5,
        "keywords": 3.5,
        "domain": 0.0,
        "chosen": false,
        "text": "Built a tool-calling LLM agent (LangChain, AWS Bedrock, Claude Haiku 4.5) for a multi-omics cancer research platform, with three tools for gene alias resolution, scoring-methodology explanation and dataset provenance."
      },
      {
        "id": "p_ch1",
